<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54303" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακτείνω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κτενέω</span>, in 3sg.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κτενεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.412
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κτᾰνέω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					6.409
				</span></i>
			: aor. 1
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέκτεινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hom.
				</span></i>
			 (in all moods but ind.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				58.7
			</span></i>, al. (Miletus, <span class="entity">v B. C.</span>): aor. 2
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέκτᾰνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.204
				</span></i>
			, etc., 
				Ep.
			 imper. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάκτανε</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				164
			</span></i>: poet. aor. 2
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέκτᾰν, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ας</span>,
			α</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.319
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				460
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				181
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				221
			</span></i>; 
				Ep.
			
			inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακτάμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					453
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακτάμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.557
				</span></i>
			; part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακτάς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				335
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.224
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				965
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				715
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέκτονα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					587
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, fut.
			
				Med.
			 in pass. sense 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακτανέεσθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.481
				</span></i>
			 codd. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κτενέεσθε</span> Cobet):
				aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατεκτάθην</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>,
				3pl.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.558
				</span></i>
			, etc.; part.
			
				Med.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακτάμενος</span> (in pass. sense) <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.106
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατθανεῖν</span> is freq.
			used as 
				Pass.
			 to this Verb:—<i>kill, slay</i>, freq. in 
				Ep.
			 and Trag., Il.cc.; rare in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.75
			</span></i>, <u>SIG</u> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Hier.</u>
				6.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.12
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
